Z-- Language Specification (lang.doc)

Sample Z-- Programs

1. Average Calculation
start
  let a = 10
  let b = 20
  let avg = 0.0
  avg = (a + b) / 2
  print("Average is: ")
  print(avg)
end

2. Fibonacci Generator
start
  let n
  print("How many Fibonacci numbers do you want?")
  input(n)
  let a = 0 
  let b = 1
  while n > 0 {
    print(a)
    let c = a + b
    a = b
    b = c
    n = n - 1
  }
end


Syntax & Snippets
Variable Declaration & Data Types

let number = 12       // integer
let name = "Alice"    // string
let score = 95.5      // float
let isActive = true   // boolean
Use let to declare variables of any type. Type is inferred based on the assigned value.

Comments
// Single-line comment

/* 
   Multi-line
   comment
*/


Control Flow
if-else

if condition {
  // statements
} else {
  // statements
}
while Loop

while condition {
  // statements
}
for Loop


for init, condition, increment {
  // statements
}
Example:


for a = 2, a < 10, a++ {
  print(a)
}


Loop Control
break Keyword
Used to exit loops prematurely.

Example:


start
  let n = 10
  while n > 0 {
    if n == 5 {
      break
    }
    print(n)
    n = n - 1
  }
end

Functions
Defined using fun keyword.

Syntax:

fun functionName {
  arg = (param1, param2, ...)
  // function body
  return expression
}
Example:

fun solve {
  arg = (a, b)
  return a + b
}

solve(5, 3);


Operators

Logical & Bitwise
&& → Logical AND
|| → Logical OR
| → Bitwise OR
& → Bitwise AND
^ → Bitwise XOR
% → Modulo (remainder)


Notes
Strings are enclosed in double quotes " ".
input(var) is used for user input.
Semicolons are not required.
Blocks are enclosed in { }.
The program begins with start and ends with end.
